// Layer_Data_Governance — Data Governance Layer (layer 6 of 9)
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "Layer_Data_Governance".
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/Layer_Data_Governance.png
// Icons: product logos from docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked 2026-07-11):
//   airflow, spark, clickhouse, postgres, minio, kafka, dbt, opensearch;
//   the rest are generic icons. Ingest edges follow the metadata flow direction from
//   source to catalog; DataHub writes its search index to OpenSearch.
// Reference: subsec:lapisan-tata-kelola (Section IV.3, sec:arsitektur-terintegrasi);
//   tool detail for the layer in row 6 of tab:layanan_industri, which details the same
//   layer as Figure fig:integrate-service (Section IV.1).
//   Included in LaTeX as fig:layer-governance.
// Focus: DataHub (catalog + lineage GMS) receives OpenLineage events from Airflow
//   and Spark plus ingest from ClickHouse, PostgreSQL, MinIO, Kafka, Feast, and dbt;
//   Great Expectations as the quality gate inside the pipeline, streaming
//   status to the catalog; boundary toward Observability.
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right): metadata sources as the left column,
//   DataHub in the middle, at most two rows of nodes per group, so the diagram widens and
//   fits the height=0.42\textheight band. Included without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Layer basis: the group label carries its source annotation, namely data quality, data
//   testing, and data governance (munappy2020adhoc, rella2022mlops,
//   jain2025integrating) per row 6 of tab:layanan_industri.
// Implementation check: DataHub = data-governance/datahub + datahub-ingestion,
//   Great Expectations = data-processing/great-expectations, OpenSearch =
//   data-governance/opensearch. OpenLineage = the lineage event protocol
//   emitted by Airflow and Spark (not a standalone component directory, cited openlineage2025).

direction right

// Lineage-emitting pipeline sources (boundary)
Airflow [icon: airflow, color: orange, label: "Apache Airflow (data pipeline)"]
Spark [icon: spark, color: orange, label: "Apache Spark (batch)"]

// Metadata ingest sources (boundary)
Platform Metadata Sources [icon: database, color: green, label: "Platform Metadata Sources"] {
  ClickHouse [icon: clickhouse, label: "ClickHouse"]
  PostgreSQL [icon: postgres, label: "PostgreSQL"]
  MinIO [icon: minio, label: "MinIO + Iceberg"]
  Kafka [icon: kafka, label: "Kafka"]
  Feast [icon: package, label: "Feast"]
  dbt [icon: dbt, label: "dbt"]
}

// Data governance section
Data Governance Layer [icon: book, color: teal, label: "Data Governance Layer (data quality + data testing + data governance)"] {
  DataHub [icon: book-open, label: "DataHub (catalog + lineage, GMS backend)"]
  OpenLineage [icon: git-merge, label: "OpenLineage (lineage events)"]
  Great Expectations [icon: check-square, label: "Great Expectations (quality gate)"]
}

// Index and downstream boundary
OpenSearch [icon: opensearch, color: green, label: "OpenSearch (catalog index)"]
Observability Layer [icon: monitor, color: teal, label: "Observability Layer"]

// Lineage flow
Airflow > OpenLineage: lineage events
Spark > OpenLineage: lineage events
OpenLineage > DataHub: lineage graph

// Metadata ingest flow
ClickHouse > DataHub: table ingest
PostgreSQL > DataHub: schema ingest
MinIO > DataHub: dataset ingest
Kafka > DataHub: topic ingest
Feast > DataHub: feature definition ingest
dbt > DataHub: transformation model ingest

// Quality and index flow
Airflow > Great Expectations: in-pipeline quality gate
Great Expectations > DataHub: validation status
DataHub > OpenSearch: write search index
DataHub > Observability Layer: governance signal
